@baseUrl = http://localhost:5285
# docker compose (two replicas behind nginx): @baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}
@userId = {{registerBob.response.body.$.user.id}}
@carolId = {{registerCarol.response.body.$.user.id}}
@directConversationId = {{createDirect.response.body.$.conversationId}}
@conversationId = {{createGroup.response.body.$.conversationId}}
@messageId = {{sendText.response.body.$.id}}

# Run the requests top to bottom: later requests use ids and tokens from earlier responses.
# Real-time: connect a SignalR client to {{baseUrl}}/hubs/chat?access_token={{accessToken}}
#
# Behind nginx there are no sticky sessions, so a negotiate request and the connection that follows can land on
# different replicas. Clients must skip negotiation and use WebSockets only:
#   JavaScript: new HubConnectionBuilder().withUrl(`${baseUrl}/hubs/chat`, {
#                 transport: HttpTransportType.WebSockets, skipNegotiation: true, accessTokenFactory: () => token })
#   .NET:       .WithUrl($"{baseUrl}/hubs/chat", o => { o.Transports = HttpTransportType.WebSockets;
#                 o.SkipNegotiation = true; o.AccessTokenProvider = () => Task.FromResult(token); })
# Every response carries X-Instance-Id under docker compose, showing which replica served it.
#
# The server closes a hub connection when its access token expires (15 minutes), so a revoked or deleted account
# cannot keep a socket open longer than that. Clients must reconnect with a fresh token: enable automatic reconnect
# and make the token factory return a current access token, refreshing it first when it has expired:
#   JavaScript: .withUrl(url, { ..., accessTokenFactory: () => getFreshAccessToken() }).withAutomaticReconnect()
#   .NET:       o.AccessTokenProvider = GetFreshAccessTokenAsync; builder.WithAutomaticReconnect()
# If automatic reconnect gives up (onclose), start the connection again after refreshing the token.
#
# Presence and privacy: PresenceChanged { userId, isOnline, lastSeenUtc } is only sent about users who show their last
# seen, and only to users who show their own. When someone hides theirs, peers get { isOnline: false, lastSeenUtc: null }
# at once (and the hider gets the same for each peer); when they show it again, both sides get the real state.
# Message payloads (MessageReceived, MessageUpdated, GET messages) and MemberAdded never carry presence: their
# sender/member has isOnline false and lastSeenUtc null. Read presence from the conversation list and details, user
# lookup, search and PresenceChanged. Every user summary has a "username" (null for deleted accounts).

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ───────────── Auth (per IP: register/login/reset-password 10 / minute, refresh/logout/change-password 60 / minute) ─────────────
# Every account needs a username: 3-30 characters, lowercase letters, digits, "_" and ".", starting with a letter, no two
# "." or "_" in a row, not ending with "."; stored lowercase ("Alice_99" becomes "alice_99"). Reserved names (admin,
# support, chathub, system, api, root, help, guest, bot, null, undefined, ...) are refused. Validation errors come back as
# 400 with an "errors.Username" entry; a name in use as 409 User.UsernameTaken.

# @name registerAlice
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Alice",
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": null,
  "password": "secret123"
}

###
# Phone numbers: an Egyptian mobile in local form (01001234567), without the 0 (1001234567, what a client with a fixed
# +20 prefix sends) or international (+201001234567); other countries need the full +<country code> form. Landlines and
# wrong lengths get 400 "Enter a valid Egyptian mobile number, e.g. 01001234567". Numbers are stored and matched in E.164,
# so any of these forms finds the same user at register and login. Phones are never verified (no SMS, by design).
# @name registerBob
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Bob",
  "username": "bob_builder",
  "email": null,
  "phoneNumber": "01001234567",
  "password": "secret123"
}

###
# @name registerCarol
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Carol",
  "username": "carol",
  "email": "carol@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

###
# The identifier is an email (contains "@"), else a phone number (any accepted format), else a username (any case).
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "bob_builder",
  "password": "secret123"
}

###
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refresh.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### ───────────── Email verification (request: 5 / minute per IP and 3 / hour per user; links: 30 / minute per IP) ─────────────
# Registering with an email already sends a verification email (see Mailpit, http://127.0.0.1:8025, under docker compose).
# The link in it is {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email?token=... and works once, for 24 hours. Requesting a new one
# disables the older links. GET /api/users/me shows "emailVerified". Digests are only emailed to verified addresses.

# Resend: 202 with the address and the expiry; 400 Auth.NoEmailToVerify, 409 Auth.EmailAlreadyVerified,
# 429 Auth.VerificationThrottled
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/email-verification
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# What the link in the email opens: verifies and answers with a small HTML page (success, already verified,
# expired or replaced 410, invalid 400). Paste the token from the email.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email?token=paste-the-token-from-the-email

###
# The same for a frontend that reads the token from its own page: 204, or a problem with Auth.InvalidVerificationToken,
# Auth.VerificationTokenExpired, Auth.VerificationTokenUsed or Auth.EmailAlreadyVerified.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "paste-the-token-from-the-email"
}

### ───────────── Forgot / reset password (forgot: 5 / minute per IP and 3 emails / hour per user) ─────────────
# Always 202 with the same body and at least PasswordReset:MinimumResponseMilliseconds (300 ms), whether or not the
# address belongs to an account, so the answer reveals nothing. Only an active account with this VERIFIED email gets
# "Reset your ChatHub password" (Mailpit under docker compose). Its link opens the frontend:
#   {App:FrontendBaseUrl}/reset-password?token=...   (valid 30 minutes, once; a newer request disables older links)
# 400 when the address is malformed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com"
}

###
# The frontend's /reset-password page posts the token from its URL with the new password (same rules as register).
# 204: the password is changed, every session is signed out (refresh tokens revoked, access tokens rejected, hub
# connections closed) and a "Your ChatHub password was changed" email follows. Problems: Auth.InvalidResetToken,
# Auth.ResetTokenExpired (expired or replaced by a newer link), Auth.ResetTokenUsed; 400 with errors.NewPassword.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "paste-the-token-from-the-email-link",
  "newPassword": "newsecret456"
}

### ───────────── Unsubscribe (no login; every digest email links here) ─────────────
# GET shows a confirmation page with a button and changes nothing (mail scanners open links).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/email/unsubscribe?token=paste-the-token-from-the-digest

###
# What the button and mail clients that support RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe send. Idempotent; turns digests off.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/email/unsubscribe?token=paste-the-token-from-the-digest
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

List-Unsubscribe=One-Click

### ───────────── Users ─────────────

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Alice A.",
  "bio": "Hello there",
  "avatarFileId": null,
  "removeAvatar": false
}

###
# Email digests about unread messages on or off. Verification emails are always sent.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/email-preferences
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "emailNotificationsEnabled": false
}

###
# Username availability while typing (anonymous allowed, 30 / minute per IP). Always 200:
#   { "username": "alice_2", "available": true, "reason": null }
#   reason: "invalid" | "reserved" | "taken" when not available. Nothing about the owner is returned; names of deleted
#   accounts are free again. With a token, your own current name counts as available.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/username-availability?username=Alice_2

###
# Change the username: 200 { "username": "alice.smith", "nextChangeAtUtc": "..." }. Once every
# Username:ChangeCooldownDays (14) days; the first change after registration is free, and setting the current name again
# changes nothing. Problems: 400 User.UsernameInvalid / User.UsernameReserved, 409 User.UsernameTaken,
# 429 User.UsernameChangeTooSoon (the detail says when). GET /api/users/me shows "usernameChangeAvailableAtUtc".
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/username
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "Alice.Smith"
}

###
# Last seen privacy (default true). false: nobody sees your online status or last seen (peers get a PresenceChanged
# "offline, no last seen" right away), and you no longer see anyone else's either. You always see your own.
# Typing indicators are not affected. GET /api/users/me shows "showLastSeen".
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/privacy
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "showLastSeen": false
}

###
# Matches display names (contains), usernames (exact or prefix, a leading "@" is ignored; an exact match comes first),
# an exact email or an exact phone number.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/search?query=bob&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/search?query=@bob_b
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{carolId}}/block
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/blocked
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{carolId}}/block
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ───────────── Files ─────────────
# purpose = MessageAttachment | Avatar | GroupImage. Allowed: images, audio, pdf, office documents, zip.
# The content must match the declared type (magic bytes are checked). To upload a real file use
# a body line like:  < ./samples/avatar.png

# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files?purpose=MessageAttachment
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ChatHubBoundary

--ChatHubBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

%PDF-1.4
% ChatHub sample attachment
%%EOF
--ChatHubBoundary--

###
# A message attachment's url is signed (1 hour) and downloads without a token.
GET {{baseUrl}}{{upload.response.body.$.url}}

###
# @name uploadAvatar
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files?purpose=Avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ChatHubBoundary

--ChatHubBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="avatar.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./samples/avatar.png
--ChatHubBoundary--

###
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Alice A.",
  "bio": "Hello there",
  "avatarFileId": "{{uploadAvatar.response.body.$.id}}"
}

###
# Avatars and group images are public.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files/{{uploadAvatar.response.body.$.id}}

